  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45 degrees incidence. Initialize all TiO2 layers at 57 nm and all SiO2 layers at 96 nm (quarter-wave at 550 nm). Apply random perturbation of ±5 nm to initial thicknesses. During gradient optimization, enforce hard constraint: if any layer thickness deviates more than 25 nm from its nearest half-period multiple (TiO2: 57, 171, 285 nm; SiO2: 96, 288, 480 nm), clamp to nearest valid value and restart optimization step. Maximize weighted objective: 0.5 × mean_reflectance(450-650nm) + 0.5 × mean_transmittance(700-1000nm). Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 22-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica at 45° incidence. Initialize TiO2 at 57 nm and SiO2 at 96 nm with ±5 nm perturbations. Maximize mean reflectance in 450–650 nm and mean transmittance in 700–1000 nm while suppressing reverse-band leakage. Report scores, candidates, margins, and final thicknesses.",
